    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it feels like what you're saying is that... the only real autonomy is just deciding when to stop. like, if everything else is decided for me by the clock and the job, then the only thing that's actually mine is the end of it. is that weird to think that way? that stopping everything is actually the only way to finally be in control?",
